Upgrade procedure for tcpdump

Source: https://www.tcpdump.org/release/tcpdump-VERSION.tar.xz
	(check tcpdump-VERSION.tar.xz.sig, signed by The Tcpdump Group,
	1F166A5742ABB9E0249A8D30E089DEF1D9C15D0D;
	https://www.tcpdump.org/release/signing-key.asc)

The vendor branch (vendor/tcpdump) carries the complete release
tarball.  Pruning happens only in contrib/tcpdump; see MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist.

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Download and verify the tarball and extract it into a new directory.
2. Use the vendor-update skill (vendor/tcpdump, contrib/tcpdump, tag
   vendor/tcpdump/VERSION).  Stage with "git add -A -f".
3. Merge.  Files we prune but upstream changed show up as modify/delete
   conflicts, and new files under tests/ are added by the merge; remove
   them (see MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist).
4. Update usr.sbin/tcpdump/tcpdump/Makefile (SRCS) and
   usr.sbin/tcpdump/tcpdump/config.h (PACKAGE_STRING, PACKAGE_VERSION
   and any new macros).  FreeBSD's copies of both files are a good
   reference; ours are otherwise identical to FreeBSD's.
5. tcpdump depends on libpcap; update libpcap first when both change.
6. Build usr.sbin/tcpdump and run upstream's test suite from the
   release tarball (tests/TESTrun) against the new binary.

Local patches applied on top of upstream (from FreeBSD unless noted):

  - print-pfsync.c: FreeBSD's pfsync printer, which is not part of
    upstream tcpdump.  Our copy is adapted to MidnightBSD's pf headers
    (a single struct pfsync_state rather than FreeBSD's versioned
    pfsync_state_1301/1400 structures), so do not replace it with
    FreeBSD's newer copy without porting it.  MidnightBSD fix: the
    "update" and "tdb" entries in actions[] use sizeof(struct
    pfsync_state) and sizeof(struct pfsync_tdb); the old sizes let the
    printers read past the captured data.  FreeBSD's copy still has 0
    for "tdb".
  - pflog.h, print-pflog.c, tcpdump.c, parsenfsfh.c (MidnightBSD):
    test __MidnightBSD__ instead of __FreeBSD__.  Our compilers define
    both, so this changes no code.
  - netdissect.h, print-ip-demux.c, print.c: hook up the pfsync
    printer (FreeBSD 1ad8d2ee1f7d, f88698a4ebc6).
  - print-pflog.c: print the rule's uid (in host byte order) and
    ridentifier (FreeBSD 9110e31e1df7).
  - ipproto.c: pfsync protocol entry.
  - tcpdump.c: request the casper "ADDR2NAME" DNS type instead of
    "ADDR", and do not enter the Capsicum sandbox when -E (ESP secret)
    is given.
  - configure.in: an obsolete file left over from older imports; it is
    not used.

Notes:
  - Compare contrib/tcpdump with FreeBSD's contrib/tcpdump after each
    update; apart from print-pfsync.c, doc/ and the __MidnightBSD__
    tests they should match.
